## Issue
`body.mce-content-body` (TinyMCE editor iframe editing area) should use container background, not page background.

Current state:
- next-gen/content.less: No background in light mode, hardcoded #171b21 in dark mode
- canvas/content.less: No background defined (inherits)
- canvas-high-contrast/content.less: No background defined (inherits)

Problem: The content.less files don't import generated token variables, so they can't use @background-color or other theme tokens.

## Token Semantics

From [packages/scaffold/templates/canvas-theme-editor/src/app.css#L9-L21]:
- Light mode: `--instui-color-background-container` (lighter surface for controls/cards)
- Dark mode: `--instui-color-background-page` (darkest background)

These tokens are used for the scaffold chrome's own UI layout (not preview content).

The TinyMCE editor iframe body should follow the same pattern:
- Light mode body bg: `--instui-color-background-container`
- Dark mode body bg: `--instui-color-background-page`

This matches the editor chrome aesthetic and creates visual consistency.

## Current generate.ts Architecture

**[renderers/tinymce/scripts/generate.ts:22-37]** Token mapping for skin files:
```typescript
const LESS_TOKEN_VARIABLES = [
  ["background-color", "--instui-color-background-base"],  // Used in skin.less
  // ... other mappings
]

function writeTokenVariables(name: string, theme: ThemeName, mode: "light" | "dark"): void {
  const resolved = new Map(resolveTokens(themes[theme], { mode }));
  const lines = LESS_TOKEN_VARIABLES.map(([lessName, tokenName]) => {
    const value = resolved.get(tokenName);
    if (!value) throw new Error(`Missing ${tokenName} in ${theme} ${mode} token IR`);
    return `@${lessName}: ${value}; // ${tokenName}`;
  });
  mkdirSync(generatedLessRoot, { recursive: true });
  writeFileSync(resolve(generatedLessRoot, `${name}-tokens.less`), `${lines.join("\n")}\n`);
}
```

Generates files like:
- `oxide/src/less/generated/next-gen-light-tokens.less`
- `oxide/src/less/generated/next-gen-dark-tokens.less`
- `oxide/src/less/generated/canvas-tokens.less`
- `oxide/src/less/generated/canvas-high-contrast-tokens.less`

These are imported **only in skin.less files**:
