## 3. Browser API Path for RESOLVED Mode

### getComputedStyle() Approach (Required for RESOLVED)

To resolve `var(--instui-spacing-space-xs)` → `0.75rem`:

```typescript
// Pseudo-code for browser-based resolution
export function resolveCssVariables(html: string, css: string): string {
  // 1. Create a temporary DOM with <style> + HTML
  const fragment = document.createElement("template");
  fragment.innerHTML = `<style>${css}</style>${html}`;
  document.body.appendChild(fragment.content);

  // 2. Walk elements; collect all computed style properties
  for (const element of document.querySelectorAll("*")) {
    const computed = getComputedStyle(element);
    const inlineStyle = element.getAttribute("style") || "";

    // 3. Parse existing inline styles; resolve var() references
    const resolved = new CSSStyleDeclaration();
    for (const [prop, value] of Object.entries(computed)) {
      if (inlineStyle.includes(prop)) {
        const inlineValue = element.style.getPropertyValue(prop);
        if (inlineValue.includes("var(")) {
          // Substitute from computed style
          resolved.setProperty(prop, computed.getPropertyValue(prop));
        } else {
          resolved.setProperty(prop, inlineValue);
        }
      }
    }

    // 4. Write resolved style back
    element.setAttribute("style", resolved.cssText);
  }

  // 5. Extract HTML + generate fallback stylesheet for pseudo/media
  return fragment.innerHTML;
}
```

### Critical Constraints

1. **Browser-only**: Must run in DOM context (browser >= ES2020 required for structured iteration)
2. **Pseudo-elements unreachable**: `getComputedStyle(el, "::before")` returns object, but can't extract as CSS text; pseudo rules must stay in `<style>` fallback
3. **@media/@supports unresolvable**: Must evaluate at render time; can't know user's viewport/capability upfront
4. **Timing**: Must run AFTER:
   - All stylesheets loaded (including fonts for `getComputedStyle(el).fontFamily`)
   - DOM interactive (element tree complete)
   - NO ongoing animations/transitions (affects computed color values)

