## 5. Option Framework for User Decision

### Clear Decision Tree

**Q1: Should inline mode resolve all CSS variables to computed values?**

**Option A: VAR REFERENCE (current)**
- Preserves `var(--instui-*)` throughout
- Requires companion `theme.css` with all variable declarations
- Canvas-safe: Works with TinyMCE's `editor.getContent()` + Juice fallback styling
- Limitation: User must upload BOTH theme.css + inlined theme.html (OR use "None" provider)
- API: `inlineHtml(html, css, { resolveCSSVariables: false })` — current default
- Best for: Single-file HTML export when theme.css is available separately

**Option B: RESOLVED VALUE (new)**
- Computes all variables to final CSS values: `var(--spacing-xs)` → `0.75rem`
- Single-file standalone: No theme.css needed
- Limitation: Requires browser (DOM, getComputedStyle); @media/@supports/@pseudo-elements must stay in fallback sheet
- Canvas risk: style attributes may be sanitized; test required
- API: `inlineHtml(html, css, { resolveCSSVariables: true, resolvedIn: 'browser' })` — new
- Best for: Standalone HTML for Canvas paste/email/archival where stylesheets unavailable

**Option C: HYBRID (future)**
- Resolve what's inlinable (regular custom props); keep light-dark/calc fallback vars
- Advanced; deferred unless user requests

### Recommended Q2: Browser Inlining Entry Point

**Option 1: Separate export**
```typescript
// formats/inline-styles/src/inline-html-browser.ts (NEW)
export async function inlineHtmlBrowser(
  html: string, 
  css: string, 
  options?: InlineHtmlOptions & { resolveVariables?: boolean }
): Promise<string> {
  // Only available in browser (DOM required)
  const fragment = parseHtml(html);
  const resolved = resolveInlinedVariables(fragment, css);
  return serializeHtml(resolved);
}
```
- **Exports**: `./html/browser` in package.json
- **Entry point**: `await import("@pantoken/inline-styles/html/browser")`
- **Advantage**: Tree-shaking; Node code doesn't pull browser deps
- **Drawback**: User must know when browser vs Node

**Option 2: Unified export with runtime detection**
```typescript
// formats/inline-styles/src/inline-html.ts (MODIFIED)
export function inlineHtml(
  html: string, 
  css: string, 
  options: InlineHtmlOptions & { resolvedIn?: 'node' | 'browser' } = {}
): string | Promise<string> {
  if (options.resolvedIn === 'browser' && typeof document !== 'undefined') {
    return inlineHtmlBrowser(html, css, options);
  }
  // ← fallback to Node Juice (synchronous)
  return inlineHtmlNode(html, css, options);
}
```
- **Advantage**: Single API surface; library chooses automatically
- **Drawback**: Conditional behavior; harder to test/type

### Recommended Q3: API Surface (Minimal Change)

**Proposal** (backward-compatible):

```typescript
// formats/inline-styles/src/inline-html.ts
export interface InlineHtmlOptions {
  preserveFallbacks?: boolean;  // ← existing (default true)
  resolveCSSVariables?: boolean;  // ← existing (default false)
  inlineCustomProperties?: boolean;  // ← existing (default true)

  // NEW: Opt-in resolved mode
  resolveCustomProperties?: boolean;  // (default false) — when true, resolve -- declarations
  // Future: resolvedIn?: 'node' | 'browser' — deferred until browser entry added
}

export function inlineHtml(
  html: string,
  css: string,
  options: InlineHtmlOptions = {}
): string {
  // Existing Juice path (always Node-safe, synchronous)
  const { 
    preserveFallbacks = true, 
    resolveCSSVariables = false,
    resolveCustomProperties = false  // ignored in Node; for browser compat
  } = options;

  let flatCss = flattenScopes(css);
  if (options.inlineCustomProperties === false) {
    const root = postcss.parse(flatCss);
    root.walkDecls((declaration) => {
      if (declaration.prop.startsWith("--")) declaration.remove();
    });
    flatCss = root.toString();
  }

  const safeCss = flatCss.replace(/</gu, "\\3C ");
  return juice(`<style>${safeCss}</style>${html}`, {
    preserveContainerQueries: preserveFallbacks,
    preserveFontFaces: preserveFallbacks,
    preserveKeyFrames: preserveFallbacks,
    preserveLayers: preserveFallbacks,
    preserveMediaQueries: preserveFallbacks,
    preservePseudos: preserveFallbacks,
    removeStyleTags: true,
    resolveCSSVariables,  // ← Juice's limited Node resolution
  });
}
```

**Changes**:
- ✅ Backward-compatible (no existing calls break)
- ✅ Clear naming (resolveCustomProperties vs resolveCSSVariables)
- ✅ Documented: VAR REFERENCE (false) vs RESOLVED VALUE (true, browser only)
- ✅ Tests verify behavior in both modes

**Browser entry (Phase 2)**:
```typescript
// formats/inline-styles/src/inline-html-browser.ts (NEW)
export async function inlineHtmlBrowser(
  html: string,
  css: string,
  options: InlineHtmlOptions & { resolveCustomProperties: boolean } = {}
): Promise<string> {
  // Browser-only; requires DOM + getComputedStyle
  // Implementation uses Juice client + custom variable resolution
}

// package.json export
{
  "./html": "./dist/html.mjs",
  "./html/browser": "./dist/html-browser.mjs"  // NEW
}
```

