## 6. Node vs Browser Compatibility Matrix

### Environment Detection

```typescript
const isBrowser = typeof document !== 'undefined' && typeof window !== 'undefined';
const isNode = typeof process !== 'undefined' && process.versions?.node;
```

### Feature Matrix

| Feature | Node 22.18+ | Browser ES2020+ | Canvas RCE |
|---------|------------|-----------------|-----------|
| Juice (Node path) | ✅ sync | ❌ (pulls PostCSS, fs shims) | N/A |
| Juice (Client) | N/A | ✅ async | Limited (sanitizer) |
| getComputedStyle() | ❌ (no DOM) | ✅ | ⚠️ (TinyMCE context) |
| flattenScopes (PostCSS) | ✅ | ✅ (bundled) | ✅ (bundled) |
| RESOLVED mode | ❌ (Juice insufficient) | ✅ (DOM required) | ⚠️ (TinyMCE+ Canvas sanitize) |
| VAR REFERENCE mode | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ (recommended) |

### Build Implications

**Existing**: formats/inline-styles/dist/html.mjs
- Vite config marks `juice` as external
- PostCSS bundled (no Node deps leaked)
- Node-only import `juice` (CommonJS or ESM)

**New browser entry**: formats/inline-styles/dist/html-browser.mjs
- Vite config includes Juice client (not Node entry)
- Tree-shake Node-only imports
- Async API (Promise<string>)
- Include DOMPurify-safe HTML parsing (happy-dom or custom)

**Vite config**: [formats/inline-styles/vite.config.ts](formats/inline-styles/vite.config.ts)
- Check existing build config
- Parallel entry point needed for browser build

